From a3985845c12e1d2a118a727aaef80393f21112b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anurag-r <anurag.r@focaloid.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Nov 2025 15:49:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add limit on multipart form parts to mitigate DoS attacks

This update introduces a maximum limit of 1000 multipart parts for form data parsing. If this limit is exceeded, a `RequestEntityTooLarge` exception is raised. This change aims to prevent potential denial-of-service attacks that could arise from excessive resource consumption during form processing. Additionally, documentation has been updated to reflect this new limit and its implications.
---
 CHANGES.rst                      |  9 ++++++++
 docs/request_data.rst            | 37 +++++++++++++++++---------------
 src/werkzeug/formparser.py       | 16 +++++++++++++-
 src/werkzeug/sansio/multipart.py |  8 +++++++
 src/werkzeug/wrappers/request.py |  8 +++++++
 tests/test_formparser.py         |  9 ++++++++
 6 files changed, 69 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGES.rst b/CHANGES.rst
index 41353ad9..5e23312a 100644
--- a/CHANGES.rst
+++ b/CHANGES.rst
@@ -1,5 +1,14 @@
 .. currentmodule:: werkzeug
 
+Unreleased
+----------
+
+-   Specify a maximum number of multipart parts, default 1000, after which a
+    ``RequestEntityTooLarge`` exception is raised on parsing. This mitigates a DoS
+    attack where a larger number of form/file parts would result in disproportionate
+    resource use.
+
+
 Version 2.1.2
 -------------
 
